FCM CONFIGURATION PATCHING GUIDE

This document details the procedure for syncing and porting Cirrus-specific fcm-make build configurations (e.g., ncas-cirrus-cce) between working branches using standard unified diff patches and FCM version control.

NOTE ON WORKFLOW AND VERSIONS:
In this workflow, the vn13.8 branch (vn13.8_cirrus_compile) was configured and verified manually first to serve as the reference standard. Porting these changes to your target UM version branch is controlled by setting the $VN environment variable in Step 1. The exact same procedure applies when porting these configuration diffs to any version branch (e.g., 13.9, 13.0, 13.5, 13.2, etc.).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREREQUISITES: BRANCH CREATION & CHECKOUT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Create target working branch from reference standard (e.g., vn13.8):

fcm bc cirrus_compile fcm:um.x_tr@vn13.8

Suggested commit message to paste into editor:
--------------------------------------------------
Cirrus build porting.
--------------------------------------------------

2. Checkout working copy of the new branch:

fcm co [new branch address]


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WORKFLOW: PORTING FCM-MAKE CONFIGURATIONS BETWEEN BRANCHES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 1: INITIALISE TARGET CONFIGURATION DIRECTORY

Set your target UM version (e.g., 13.9, 13.0, 13.5, 13.2) and navigate to the fcm-make directory:

export VN="13.9"

cd /home/n02/n02/jonnyhtw/branches/vn${VN}_cirrus_compile/fcm-make


STEP 2: COMMIT BASELINE TEMPLATE TO VERSION CONTROL

If the target configuration directory (e.g., ncas-cirrus-cce) does not yet exist in your target branch, use `fcm cp` to copy and stage the template configuration (e.g., ncas-ex-cce). Then commit it to establish a clean baseline commit before applying any porting patches.

# Copy template and stage for FCM version control in one step
fcm cp ncas-ex-cce ncas-cirrus-cce

# Commit the initial baseline state (opens editor for log message)
fcm commit

Suggested commit message to paste into editor:
--------------------------------------------------
Initialize ncas-cirrus-cce baseline from ncas-ex-cce template
--------------------------------------------------


STEP 3: GENERATE SCOPED CIRRUS PATCH FILE

Generate a relative unified diff from the reference branch (vn13.8_cirrus_compile) targeting strictly the 4 required configuration files:

cd /home/n02/n02/jonnyhtw/branches/vn13.8_cirrus_compile/fcm-make

# Specify exact files to diff
FILES=(
    "inc/external_paths.cfg"
    "um-atmos-debug.cfg"
    "um-atmos-high.cfg"
    "um-atmos-safe.cfg"
)

# Clear/create the patch file in the target branch
> /home/n02/n02/jonnyhtw/branches/vn${VN}_cirrus_compile/fcm-make/cirrus_config.patch

# Append diffs using relative paths
for f in "${FILES[@]}"; do
    diff -u "ncas-ex-cce/$f" "ncas-cirrus-cce/$f" >> /home/n02/n02/jonnyhtw/branches/vn${VN}_cirrus_compile/fcm-make/cirrus_config.patch
done

# Return to target branch directory
cd /home/n02/n02/jonnyhtw/branches/vn${VN}_cirrus_compile/fcm-make


STEP 4: TEST PATCH APPLICATION (DRY-RUN)

Ensure local target structure exists, then verify that all 4 target files match and the patch applies cleanly to ncas-cirrus-cce:

# Ensure target directory structure exists
mkdir -p ncas-cirrus-cce/inc

# Dry-run test targeting ncas-cirrus-cce
patch -p1 -d ncas-cirrus-cce --dry-run < cirrus_config.patch

(Note: "checking file ..." indicates that patch has verified the target files exist in ncas-cirrus-cce and that the hunk contexts match without modifying disk files.)


STEP 5: APPLY THE PATCH AND CLEAN UP

Apply the changes directly to the ncas-cirrus-cce directory, verify/adjust version-dependent paths, and remove the patch file:

# Apply patch to ncas-cirrus-cce
patch -p1 -d ncas-cirrus-cce < cirrus_config.patch
rm cirrus_config.patch

NOTE ON external_paths.cfg:
Check ncas-cirrus-cce/inc/external_paths.cfg to ensure the target branch retains its native library version (e.g. gcom8.3 for vn13.7/13.2 vs gcom8.4 for vn13.8) alongside the updated Cirrus paths.


STEP 6: COMMIT PORTED CHANGES AND CLEAN UP ENVIRONMENT

Verify working copy status, commit the applied diffs directly from the fcm-make directory, and clean up the shell environment variable:

# Verify working copy status (modified 'M')
fcm st

# Commit the ported configuration changes (opens editor for log message)
fcm commit

Suggested commit message to paste into editor:
--------------------------------------------------
Port ncas-cirrus-cce build configurations from vn13.8 reference branch
--------------------------------------------------

# Unset environment variable
unset VN
